 I still thinks that &quot;<i>Forsaken by Rome</i>&quot; is more interesting Era - we have still working Rome, but players play a civilized &quot;barbarians&quot; left by the Empire to work the mess of clashing cultures of homeland and &quot;civilization&quot; they were introduced - opposing both Rome and other, real barbarians. It is great metaphor for the werewolves society at large, and highly marking themes of both savage fury and the hunt of the game. We probably see how Tribes are developing in Europe, what would nicely add to the historical depth of the <b>Werewolf</b> in general. And we have all the pagan gods to look over for our Packs, still making mess across continent. Not to mentioned obvious crossovers with <b>Requiem for Rome</b>. I will not exaggerated if I say that this era can be <b>Werewolf</b> equivalent of <i>To The Strongest </i><b>Mage</b> one - and that setting is absolutely brilliant!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T14:29:42-08:00","id":396783,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Mage and Demon are really popular but haven't been put up against each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T15:01:37-08:00","id":396806,"title":"","content":"Fucking hell, yo