rkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/394903-dark-eras-forsaken-by-rome-needs-your-votes?p=396881#post396881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking as the guy who voted for the Vampire setting, the Geist setting, and the Innocents setting....Well, fuck, do I even need to add commentary to that?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I feel your pain. *voted for Werewolf and Innocents and Hunter*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>GM of the <i>Walking Shadow</i> Campaigns</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/8992-the-hacks-and-houserules-of-walking-shadows\" target=\"_blank\">New System and Setting Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1040-neotiamat","name":"NeoTiamat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"471"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T16:21:52-08:00","id":396894,"title":"","content":"There ya go!<br /> <br /> Now I need to get back to ardently fighting against you all, but keep up the good fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T16:23:45-08:00","id":396896,"title":"","content":"The first post in this thread makes it sound like I said this is the last chance for a <i>Werewolf</i> era. I didn't. I don't actually know what the polls are much further in the future than you do, because we're making the decisions as we go. <i>Werewolf</i> could come up for another era. One of the runners-up could also come back in another poll. And <i>Forsaken</i> might yet pull ahead in this one -- the lead has swapped back and forth a few times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T16:28:00-08:00","id":396900,"title":"","content":"Yeah there's still almost three weeks left, and we've been going through stretch goals at like, one every three days or so? Plus I think there tends to be some jumps in backing near the end of the period.<br /> <br /> But still, just based on the numbers we've seen it looks like Mage is going to beat Werewolf which will beat Geist. And Demon will beat Werewolf which will beat Hunter. I'm still surprised Changeling won in the first poll, but I think it was more due to how the poll originally presented the eras.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T16:39:31-08:00","id":396916,"title":"","content":"Nah, Changeling is just that popular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T17:05:42-08:00","id":396956,"title":"","content":"I don't think there's a fixed hierarchy of games that will win polls, determined by absolute levels of popularity. The way we've seen the polls end, and the way we've seen them change during their runs, suggests otherwise.<br /> <br /> I'll have more to say about this once we're further into the KS, but right now it looks to me like votes come in the same surges as backers, and those surges sometimes swing the polls. I suspect this is due to people spreading the KS and poll links. But I'm really not sure yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T17:40:26-08:00","id":396991,"title":"","content":"I voted for werewolf! And the results are 40% werewolf and 43% Demon. Though I still feel the sting when Vikings lost <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T17:50:03-08:00","id":397003,"title":"","content":"Werewolf has been slowly creeping back up over the day. Unless the weird morning Demon-surge happens again, we might see the gap close before the polls close.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T17:57:29-08:00","id":397012,"title":"","content":"Wow people got negative nancy here while I wasn't looking.<br /> <br /> Seriously people it's not the end of the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T19:42:02-08:00","id":397082,"title":"","content":"Oh, I'm still all for the Werewolf rally, I was just commenting on the poll pairings and sharing my feelings. Against any other group, aside from Changeling, Werewolf would have run away with the every poll we've been in. As it stands, we've been set against two of the most beloved splats, in very awesome eras, and we finish with an <i>incredibly </i>strong second place showing. I'm proud of what we've done, but I am a little worried because second place isn't quite good enough to get in the book.<br /> <br /> The third option is a spoiler, currently holding 250+ votes which would otherwise swing the vote massively. I'd be curious what a two choice poll might look like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T19:57:20-08:00","id":397119,"title":"","content":"I was thinking something similar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T20:09:17-08:00","id":397123,"title":"","content":"I think expressing disappointment when it doesn't look like you're going to win is natural, it's happened on this very forum from people who tried gathering votes for Innocents. And no one's said anything about 'the end of the world.' We still have a core book coming at some point. And while we haven't won yet Werewolf's gotten the second most votes in the two most heavily voted polls, one of which isn't over. But once you've voted and gotten other people to vote, there is little to do but wait and occasionally talk about it.<br /> <br /> It might be more of a case of exaggerating elliots.<br /> <br /> Anyways, I suppose a topic to talk about might be what you'd want to see in Roman barbarian werewolves. As someone who doesn't know much about Rome's neighbors it seems like they had a ton of barbarian neighbors, like the Celts, the Goths, the Huns, the Persians and even Numidians and others in North Africa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-07-2015, 11:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T20:31:51-08:00","id":397137,"title":"","content":"The goths were pushed out by the huns, into Roman territory (this is 3rd century mind you) which was when they eventually sacked and conquered themselves a kingdom. That came about from the Romans treating them like slave beasts and lower then humans. Instances of forcing them to sell their children into slavery for dog meat to eat was apparently pretty common. Then 3 major leaders got together and decided they weren't taking it anymore and started kicking ass. Stole a bunch of roman gear off dead romans, and later met up with emperor Valens at the battle of Adriannople. He died, along with 2/3rds of the Roman army. Smashed by Fritigern's infantry and his fellow commanders mounted cavalry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T20:58:20-08:00","id":397151,"title":"","content":"I know the Huns managed to sack a lot of northern Italy, but didn't quite get Rome. But it seems like the era wouldn't take place in a specific war, if only because it would limit options of what to do.<br /> <br /> And yes, he sounds like a Storm Lord.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-08-2015, 12:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T22:24:44-08:00","id":397207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/394903-dark-eras-forsaken-by-rome-needs-your-votes?p=397123#post397123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think expressing disappointment when it doesn't look like you're going to win is natural, it's happened on this very forum from people who tried gathering votes for Innocents. And no one's said anything about 'the end of the world.' We still have a core book coming at some point. And while we haven't won yet Werewolf's gotten the second most votes in the two most heavily voted polls, one of which isn't over. But once you've voted and gotten other people to vote, there is little to do but wait and occasionally talk about it.<br /> <br /> It might be more of a case of exaggerating elliots.<br /> <br /> Anyways, I suppose a topic to talk about might be what you'd want to see in Roman barbarian werewolves. As someone who doesn't know much about Rome's neighbors it seems like they had a ton of barbarian neighbors, like the Celts, the Goths, the Huns, the Persians and even Numidians and others in North Africa.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And I suppose I was getting a little negative about the negativity because I feel negative about the possibility of werewolf losing again.<br /> <br /> Huh. So I guess I'm the nancy. Oops.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T22:49:24-08:00","id":397220,"title":"","content":"Maybe it's me starting this downer spiral, but when you vote twice on <b>Werewolf</b> and once on <b>Innocents</b> - and in all the polls you get second place - it is <i><b>a big</b></i> downer. At least mine <b>Changeling</b> passed, but I still think the <b>Werewolf</b> more deserve truly historical setting, because he get almost modern one in main <b>Dark Eras</b> book, in contrast to other major gamelines.<br /> <br /> And it is a real risk of last poll for <b>Werewolf</b> as KS is getting more and more slowly the funds - there is limited amounts of fans who can back project and we are almost in area of 2nd value of starting sum. I just say we probably mark now Stretch Goal, next one about expanded material on previous Eras, and maybe one more. Seeing how polls are putted, it can be really last one for Wolves.<br /> <br /> At least if really one last Stretch Goal would be come back of &quot;second best Eras&quot;, were we will have one <b>Vampire</b> and two <b>Werewolf</b> ones ( and, maybe, <b>Innocents</b>). In that scenario I will do not know on what to vote for - both <b>Werewolf</b> Eras are appealing, but to win, we must focus on one. And I will be partially heart broken with letting <b>Innocents</b> past. But I whole heartily believe <b>Werewolf</b> should get second Era, just to see how it will be working in the pre-modern setting. WW2 children will play, mostly, like now days children - werewolves will be other beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-08-2015, 01:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T23:05:40-08:00","id":397230,"title":"","content":"At the risk of being a reasonable randi, or heaven forfend, an optimistic ollie, neither the kickstarter or the poll are over yet. And there's 20 days left so far. We'll probably see a few more polls before it's all up. And it looks like Rose is keeping track of numbers so the fact that Werewolf has oodles of voters isn't unknown to Onyx Path.<br /> <br /> I think I heard someone say that it's common for there to be less backing on the weekend, but who knows.<br /> <br /> Just be sure to vote. Ask your friends and family to vote. Ask them to get their friends to vote.<br /> <br /> If all else fails, we haven't technically lost anything and we're still getting our new rulebook at some point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachm