div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/394903-dark-eras-forsaken-by-rome-needs-your-votes?p=400186#post400186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm gonna say that To the Strongest is the best core era, followed by Requiem for Regina. Because they explain things that have impact. Bowery Dogs is cool, but it doesn't actually tell us anything about the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not a fan of having the world described in detail beyond what I need to run a game. <i>Bowery Dogs</i> does that while staying laser-focused on the details that are important for that setting. Things I don't ever, <i>ever</i> want printed in books are pointless historical details.<br /> <br /> Which sounds strange, I'm sure, given that this whole kickstarter is about extra historical detail for games, but I promise it makes sense in my brain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.th